 "verdict": "Targeting is fixed: plain right-click, Shift+right-click, A+left-click and Z fighters-only picks were right in every trial, across 2 archers and 2 casters, after 4 min. There was also zero movement without a command over ~62k traced frames. The pathing half of the owner complaint still reproduces live, so this fails. A held right button through a packed lane fight (dunsom, 8:15, ally tower plus a standing ally wave between hero and point) ping-ponged the hero back and forth ~1.5 m with 5 reversals in 4 s. It never gained ground, and the order gave up 8.4 m short of the held point. A second held move was pinned against a wall by an enemy clump: it crawled at ~0.25 m/s for 4 s and ended 2.7 m short. To a player this reads as \"runs around on its own\" and \"stops short\", the exact complaint. Ruling 38 claims 0 such cases in packed fights after 3:55.",
